tion":"Use this cell to create links to other sets","type":"set_link","additional_fields":{"set-id":"12795f716d6d6d8d05250300","class":"hide-description"},"id":"b17b5f716d6d6d8d056b0300","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/full/screen-shot-2013-06-12-at-4.26.23-pm.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/small/screen-shot-2013-06-12-at-4.26.23-pm.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/medium/screen-shot-2013-06-12-at-4.26.23-pm.png"}},"x":6,"y":0,"width":4,"height":1},{"title":"Score text","description":"","type":"iframe","additional_fields":{"iframe-src":"http://lab.motionbank.org/dhay/text/score-text.html"},"id":"b57b5f716d6d6d8d056c0300","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/screen-shot-2013-05-18-at-9.39.08-am-2.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/screen-shot-2013-05-18-at-9.39.08-am-2.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/screen-shot-2013-05-18-at-9.39.08-am-2.png"}},"x":6,"y":1,"width":2,"height":5},{"title":"Jeanine Durning and Ros Warby Insights","description":"Use this cell to create links to other sets","type":"set_link","additional_fields":{"set-id":"7e6e5f716d6d6d8d05e60100","class":"hide-description"},"id":"c37b5f716d6d6d8d056f0300","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/full/screen-shot-2013-06-12-at-4.40.14-pm.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/small/screen-shot-2013-06-12-at-4.40.14-pm.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/medium/screen-shot-2013-06-12-at-4.40.14-pm.png"}},"x":10,"y":1,"width":3,"height":1},{"title":"'No Time to Fly' Overlays","description":"All 21 versions (seven from each performer) with the silhouettes overlaid according to spatial position","type":"recording","additional_fields":{"xxx-videoId":"286","xxx-content-url":"modules/flowplayer/index.html","xxx-file-name":"20130601_all","iframe-src":"http://lab.motionbank.org/dhay/flowplayer/?vid=69444&file=20130601_all&gid=24","autoload":"0","solo":"24","attr-allowfullscreen":"allowfullscreen","attr-mozallowfullscreen":"mozallowfullscreen","attr-webkitallowfullscreen":"webkitallowfullscreen","css-background-color":"white"},"id":"534c33ad6d303479605c0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/001008.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/001008.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/001008.png"}},"x":2,"y":1,"width":4,"height":4},{"title":"My body quote","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<p>\"My body is limited in what it can do so I’m not interested in what it can do. I’m interested in how I can raise the threshold of my attention and energy when I break it down to the cellular body. And it’s the whole body at once. All that cellular body is contained, like in a <strong>silhouette</strong>, of the human body. (...) And it's the multi-cellular body I attend to when I'm dancing.\"<br>Deborah Hay lecture to score team February 2011</p>"},"id":"535159f16d30347d6e070000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":15,"y":4,"width":2,"height":2},{"title":"Discovering patterns text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>Discovering patterns in Deborah Hay's work</h1><p>\"… for somebody who feels like I’ve been spending the last 40 years of my life undoing the continuity of my patterning, I am shocked by the amount of patterns that are emerging.\" Deborah Hay Interview June 2012</p>"},"id":"5354e2e86d30347d6e0c0000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":13,"y":1,"width":2,"height":2},{"title":"Old title cell style (do not delete)","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<style>.cell.type-html *::-moz-selection {background-color:#dddddd !important} .cell.type-html *::selection {background-color:#dddddd !important} .cell.type-html .content {font-weight:normal} .cell.type-html h1 {text-transform: uppercase;font-size: 1.4em;font-weight: 300;letter-spacing: 0.1em;line-height: 1.3;} .cell.type-html {padding:2.5em !important;background-color:white;color:black !important;} .cell.type-html h1 {color:black;text-transform:uppercase;font-family: 'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-weight:300} .cell.type-html a {text-decoration:underline} .cell.type-html.cell-width-0,  .cell.type-html.cell-width-50 { padding: 0.5em; font-size: 25%; } .cell.type-html.cell-width-100 { padding: 0.5em; font-size: 50%; } .cell.type-html.cell-width-150 { padding: 0.75em; font-size: 58%; } .cell.type-html.cell-width-200 { padding: 1em; font-size: 66%; } .cell.type-html.cell-width-250 { padding: 1em; font-size: 74%; } .cell.type-html.cell-width-300 { padding: 1.25em; font-size: 82%; } .cell.type-html.cell-width-350 { padding: 1.25em; font-size: 90%; }</style>","css-display":"none"},"id":"5354ea2a6d30347d71150000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":0,"y":0,"width":1,"height":1},{"title":"Basic information about the contents of the site","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1><strong>using the sky</strong></h1><p>holds material developed by approaching Deborah Hay's work from three main directions. One direction was <a href=\"#/set/movement-character\">analytic</a>, based on data collected from as many performance <a href=\"#/set/april-2011-nttf-solo-recordings\">recordings</a> as possible. Another was intuitive, an <a href=\"#/set/digital-adaptation-of-no-time-to-fly\">artistic</a> response to what was learned about Deborah's process. The third direction is based on interviews focused on <a href=\"#/set/introduction-to-concepts\">concepts</a> and <a href=\"#/set/jeanine-ros-insights\"> insights</a>.</p>"},"id":"535944806d30347d71230000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":0,"y":2,"width":2,"height":2},{"title":"Juliette Mapp","description":"This recording shows Juliette Mapp performing the solo \"No Time To Fly\".","type":"recording","additional_fields":{"xxx-recording":"D03T03","xxx-videoId":"251","xxx-content-url":"modules/flowplayer/index.html","xxx-file-name":"D03T03_Juliette_sync_AJA_1","iframe-src":"http://lab.motionbank.org/dhay/flowplayer/?rec=D03T03&vid=69390&file=D03T03_Juliette_sync_AJA_1&gid=24&perf=juliettemapp","autoload":"0","solo":"24","attr-allowfullscreen":"allowfullscreen","attr-mozallowfullscreen":"mozallowfullscreen","attr-webkitallowfullscreen":"webkitallowfullscreen","class":"hide-description"},"id":"535945ad6d30347d74300000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/record-9a-1.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/record-9a-1.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/record-9a-1.jpg"}},"x":0,"y":4,"width":1,"height":1},{"title":"Describing the overlays content","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<p>Deborah Hay's written score 'No Time to Fly' was given to Jeanine Durning, Juliette Mapp and Ros Warby to create their own solo adaptations. Each adaptation was recorded seven times. Read about the <a href=\"http://motionbank.org/en/content/deborah-hay\" target=\"_blank\">score making process</a> or go to a short <a href=\"http://motionbank.org/en/event/online-scores-tutorial\" target=\"_blank\">video tour</a> of USING THE SKY.</p>"},"id":"535948a06d30347d74310000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":1,"y":0,"width":3,"height":1},{"title":"Jeanine Durning Quote","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<p>\"It's a choreography of perception, of attention and relation in time and space.\" Jeanine Durning, interview April 2013</p>"},"id":"535a1a906d30347d6e1d0000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":9,"y":5,"width":2,"height":1},{"title":"Description of what happens in the overlays.","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>The overlays are aligned …</h1><p>… with the sequence of the score text to the right. Watch the individual dancers begin then appear to wait for the others before starting the next part of the score.</p>"},"id":"535a2a016d30347d74320000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":3,"y":5,"width":3,"height":1},{"title":"Linking to General Information","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>this site scrolls horizontally</h1><p>See <a href=\"#/set/general-information\">General Information</a> for more details.</p>"},"id":"535a3dd36d30347d71240000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":0,"y":5,"width":2,"height":1},{"title":"Tutorial Link Text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1><a href=\"http://motionbank.org/de/event/online-scores-tutorial\" target=\"_blank\">LINK TO TUTORIALS</a></h1><p>Find a short video tour of USING THE SKY and suggestions on how to explore the materials here.</p>"},"id":"535a434d6d30347d771a0000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":15,"y":0,"width":2,"height":1}]}